NAME
       dmesg - print the kernel log

SYNOPSIS
       dmesg [-n lines]

DESCRIPTION
       Prints the kernel ring buffer: driver probes, mounts, faults and
       everything else the kernel has logged since boot.

OPTIONS
       -n N   show only the last N lines

EXAMPLES
       dmesg | grep hda
       dmesg -n 40

NOTES
       The log level threshold can be changed at runtime from the F2
       debug monitor with the L key, which also controls how much
       reaches the serial port.

SEE ALSO
       sysmon(1), lspci(1)
